Okay, evaluating the **Mercedes-Benz A-Class 'AMG Edition'**.

First, it's important to understand that "AMG Edition" is typically not a standalone model like the A180, A250, A35, or A45 S. Instead, it usually refers to a **special edition package** or trim level offered for a limited time, often based on an existing model (like an A250 with AMG Line, or sometimes the actual A35 or A45 S). These editions usually bundle specific cosmetic features (unique paint, wheels, aerodynamic elements, interior trim) and optional equipment.

Since the specific base model for the "AMG Edition" isn't specified, and these editions often enhance the visual appeal and feature set of mid-to-high range models, I will base this evaluation on the **Mercedes-AMG A35 4MATIC (most recent facelifted version with MHEV)**. This represents a true AMG model that often receives such "Edition" treatments. The ratings will be very similar to the standard A35, with slight adjustments reflecting the potentially higher cost and bundled features/aesthetics typical of an "Edition" package.

